# Domain Glossary

Use this glossary to keep project-domain language consistent across requirements, specs, code names, reviews, and handoffs.

## Policy

- Prefer the canonical term in user-facing docs, specs, code identifiers, tests, task-board entries, and session summaries.
- When the user uses multiple names for the same concept, stop and confirm whether they are the same concept before implementation.
- When a user claim conflicts with current code, docs, or specs, record the conflict and resolve which source is authoritative before implementation.
- Record source evidence with paths, issue links, user confirmation, or ADR/RFC references.
- Keep this file concise. Move long explanations to specs, ADRs, or feature docs and link them here.

